// A native-lane program that drives the real CUDA driver API through the
// libcuda.so.1 rows: cuInit, device+context, PTX module load, function
// handle, device allocations, host-to-device copies, an 11-argument
// cuLaunchKernel of a 4-element vector add, a context synchronize, a
// device-to-host readback checked exactly, and the teardown. It also calls
// one glibc row (getuid), so the image is the mixed import: two DT_NEEDED
// entries and the glibc version tables. Run on a host with a GPU and
// libcuda.so.1 it exits 42; each failing step exits its own number.
// The driver keeps threads after the call, so each exit is exit_group:
// a thread-only exit would leave the process running.
